y as a whole. From our team of Yoga lovers to you, thank you.</p>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<footer class=\\\"site-footer\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    &copy; YogaDirect &middot; <a href=\\\"/contact\\\">Contact Us</a> &middot; <a href=\\\"/shipping\\\">Shipping</a> &middot; <a href=\\\"/returns\\\">Returns</a> &middot; <a href=\\\"/wholesale\\\">Wholesale</a>\\n  </div>\\n</footer>\\n\\n</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Added a persistent header with search, category nav, cart link and a Shop Best Sellers button.\",\"Why\":\"Constant access to search, categories and cart reduces friction and drives more purchases.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass952F3C73\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"The fetch is returning plain text instead of HTML, so I'll need to reconstruct a proper page structure from the content I have. Let me try fetching again to see if I can get the original HTML with better formatting.I'm reconstructing the page with a sticky header that includes search functionality, category navigation, a cart link, and a \"Shop Best Sellers\" button. I'll also compute DJB2 hashes over the concatenated What and Why strings to track this improvement.\n\nComputing DJB2 hash... Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters, tracking the modulo arithmetic as values exceed the 32-bit limit. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters in \"sisten\", multiplying by 33, taking modulo 2^32, and adding each character's ASCII value to accumulate the final hash. Continuing the hash computation for the remaining characters, working through the multiplications and modulo operations to track the running hash value as each character is processed. Continuing the hash calculations for the remaining characters... Continuing the hash calculation through the remaining characters, working through 's', 'e', and 'a' with their ASCII values and modular arithmetic operations. Continuing the hash calculations through the remaining