vision, which gives me 0xAE1FC272, and I'm now identifying this as Hash4 with the class label HDLmClassAE1FC272. Moving on to the next item which involves character encoding for \"Email offerCaptures leads\". Continuing the hash calculations through the remaining characters, applying the DJB2 algorithm with modular arithmetic adjustments at each step to keep the values within bounds. Continuing through the sequence with more iterations, computing products and differences at each step to track the pattern. Now I'm computing hash 6 for \"Reviews sectionAdds proof\" by processing each character's ASCII value through the DJB2 algorithm, starting with the initial hash value and iterating through the string. Continuing through iterations 10-15, computing modular arithmetic operations with successive multiplications and differences to track the evolving values. Continuing through iterations 21-25, computing the modular arithmetic operations and tracking remainders, then converting the final result to hexadecimal and performing the division to extract the quotient.\n\nNow I'm building out the HTML structure with all the key sections—header, navigation, promotional banner, hero section, product categories, featured items with pricing and ratings, trust indicators, the original about text, customer reviews, and an email signup form.  I'll also add a wholesale call-to-action and footer, plus a sticky mobile button for conversions. I'm applying the hash class to relevant elements throughout and writing inline CSS to keep the styling compact.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The fetch only gave me plain text instead of HTML, so I'll need to construct a full conversion-optimized page from scratch for YogaDirect. I'm building out a complete site with a hero section featuring a strong value proposition and call-to-action, adding a free shipping threshold indicator, trust badges, product showcase with pricing and cart buttons, wholesale options, an email signup