ltiplied by 33. Continuing through characters r, s, i, o, and n, applying the same modular arithmetic operations with successive multiplications by 33, additions, and subtractions of powers of 2^32 to keep values in range. 1551686736 - 1543503872 = 8182864, and I'm working through the remaining hex digits by dividing by successive powers of 16, getting 7, C, D, C, 5 with no remainder, so the full hex conversion is 5C7DCC5.\n\nI'm verifying this by adding back all the components: 1543503872 + 7340032 + 786432 + 53248 + 3072 + 80 = 1551686736, which checks out. So Hash1 is HDLmClass5C7CDC50.\n\nNow I'm looking at the second improvement about adding an aggregate rating summary bar with visible ratings and review counts, which is 89 characters, so I need to condense it while keeping the core message intact.\n\nCalculating hash values for \"Added a star rating summary bar\" and \"Visible ratings build instant trust\"... Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters, working through the modular arithmetic for each step in the string processing. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters: u, m, m, a, and the start of r, applying the same modular arithmetic pattern with successive multiplications by 33 and subtractions of powers of 2^32. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters in \"Visible ratings build instant trust\", processing each letter through the rolling hash algorithm with modular arithmetic to keep values bounded. Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters, processing 'e', space, 'r', and 'a' with the same multiply-by-33-and-modulo pattern. Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters, processing the space character and then 'b', 'u', and into 'i', applying the rolling hash formula with modular arithmetic at each step. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters: 'n' produces 1826042713, 's' gives 4285627450, 't' yields 3